That archived SDSS-I/II page also asks that commercial use of data from the
SDSS public archive be approved by the Astrophysical Research Consortium. The
current SDSS pages cited above do not repeat that condition.

The bundled spectra are trimmed to the wavelength range all four share,
averaged three adjacent samples into one and stored as 16-bit integers. There
is no smoothing, normalization, resampling or shift to rest wavelength. Every
processing step, each archive URL, and SHA-256 checksums of both the CSV the
archive served and the flux as committed are recorded beside the data in
js/data/spectra/sdssSpectraProvenance.js. `npm run spectra:provenance`
regenerates both files from the archive CSVs and compares byte for byte.

Primary reference: Almeida et al. (2023), ApJS 267, 44,
doi:10.3847/1538-4365/acda98
